In the transition from Isabelle_DOF 2025 to Isabelle_DOF 2026,
the most relevant facts are:

Major Changes:

- DOF : substantially improved performance due to deeper use of Isabelle's
        parallelization mechanisms. This includes a revision of the DOF core,
        which is now closer to modern Isabelle Versions,
- DOF : Support of "targets" in text*(in tgt)<< ... >> and related commands,
- COL : more customized macros, 
- COL : native support of grid-tables,
- Manuals : A 30 page User-Manual aside with the Reference-Manual, and
- Ontologies : A new Exercise Ontology

Minor Changes:
- DOF : instances of commands with a target, text* (in L) or Theorem* (in L), stay
        global (before, they were registered as "L.oid" and could not be found),
- DOF : the document engine "dof" can be used by sessions outside the Isabelle_DOF
        hierarchy via an engine-only component (see README_DEVELOPMENT.md),
- COL : the shortcut \<^isabelle> (Isabelle/HOL) joins the other shortcuts and macros,
        and the examples use them (\<^eg>, \<^ie>, \<^etc>, \<^center>),
- COL : grid-table cells may consist of a single symbol such as \<checkmark>,
- Exercise : one source is typeset for students, professors and examiners
        via Isabelle's document variants (document_variants in the ROOT file),
- Examples : revised; new Example-III (operational semantics of CSP, session
        parent HOL-CSP_OpSem), which uses the target feature,
- Isabelle_DOF-Proofs : not yet ported; it depends on the AFP entry
        Metalogic_ProofChecker, which does not build with Isabelle 2026 (RC2),
- README, README_DEVELOPMENT, CITATION : updated; the SCP paper is the
        recommended citation.
